{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "## Lost in Translation (and Loving It) - My Japan Adventure!\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It’s a country of stunning contrasts – ancient temples nestled amongst futuristic skyscrapers, serene gardens juxtaposed with bustling city streets. Honestly, it felt like stepping into another world.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Shibuya Crossing was mesmerizing, and exploring the vibrant Harajuku district was a feast for the eyes. I devoured ramen (seriously, the best I’ve ever had!) and wandered through peaceful Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train – so efficient!) to Kyoto. The traditional atmosphere here was captivating.  Visiting Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates was a truly unforgettable experience.  I spent hours wandering through Gion, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha. \n\nThe food was a highlight everywhere.  From delicate sushi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was an adventure.  And the politeness of the people?  Unmatched.  \n\nJapan is a country that stays with you.  It’s a place where tradition and modernity coexist beautifully, offering something for everyone.  I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.002083513652905822}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.1602703034877777}, {"token": "▁Translation", "logprob": -0.00042083943844772875}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.3305834233760834}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.0006382812280207872}, {"token": "▁Loving", "logprob": -0.0003184764937032014}, {"token": "▁It", "logprob": -0.00026794656878337264}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -1.6038875579833984}, {"token": "▁-", "logprob": -0.18841712176799774}, {"token": "▁My", "logprob": -0.24401137232780457}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob